ared with 9% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 36 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,450 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the presence of multiple awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across December and verify if multiple contracts served the same purpose. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or product, which might indicate a pattern of procurement.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["4BmRj8%2Bc0MnXOjazN1Dw9Q%3D%3D","wBryGTK%2BityLAncw3qdZkA%3D%3D","cDnJpDqSzg4%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}